<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urzana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urzana was king of Musasir, a small mountain state between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and Urartu famous for the temple of the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haldi">Haldi</a>. His letters to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> of Assyria survive. During <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a>'s eighth campaign in 714 BCE he fled, and the Assyrians sacked his city and temple, carrying off a vast treasure recorded in Sargon's account and shown on a relief at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorsabad">Khorsabad</a>.</p></div>
